ame like `test-hello-world.yml`\\n- Save the workflow as `ci/test-hello-world.yml`, not under `.github/workflows/`: this repository's token cannot push workflow files, so the test harness copies it there and runs it\\n\\n## Definition of Done\\n- [ ] Program file created with correct extension\\n- [ ] Code prints \\\"Hello, World!\\\" exactly\\n- [ ] Code is properly commented\\n- [ ] Code follows Scala conventions\\n- [ ] Instructions for running the program are included (if needed)\\n- [ ] GitHub Actions workflow created and passing\\n- [ ] CI badge showing build status (optional but recommended)\\n\\n__formal_ai_exit=0\\n\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"Let me update Main.scala for you.\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call_ecbd7a9366dd414a\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"write\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"content\\\":\\\"// scalac Main.scala\\\\n// scala Main\\\\n// Emit the requested text followed by a newline.\\\\nobject Main {\\\\n  def main(args: Array[String]): Unit = {\\\\n    println(\\\\\\\"Hello, World!\\\\\\\")\\\\n  }\\\\n}\\\\n\\\",\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1792181377879/Main.scala\\\"}\"}}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call_ecbd7a9366dd414a\",\"content\":\"\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"Let me update tests/verify-output.sh for you.\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call_789b33faa9c0f330\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"write\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"content\\\":\\\"#!/bin/sh\\\\nset -eu\\\\nverification_dir=$(mktemp -d)\\\\ntrap 'rm -f \\\\\\\"$verification_dir/expected\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"$verification_dir/actual\\\\\\\"; rmdir \\\\\\\"$verification_dir\\\\\\\"' EXIT HUP INT TERM\\\\nprintf '%s\\\\\\\\n' 'Hello, World!' > \\\\\\\"$verification_dir/expected\\\\\\\"\\\\nscala Main > \\\\\\\"$verification_dir/actual\\\\\\\"\\\\ncmp \\\\\\\"$verification_dir/expected\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"$verification_dir/actual\\\\\\\"\\\\ncat \\\\\\\"$verification_dir/actual\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\",\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/tmp